  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
